# Requests for every scenario. Run the API first (dotnet run --project ResultUnion.WebApi),
# then send these from Visual Studio, Rider or VS Code (REST Client). Scalar UI: http://localhost:5258/scalar

@api = http://localhost:5258

### 201 Created
POST {{api}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "bob@example.com", "password": "s3cret!pass", "age": "29" }

### 400: every invalid field at once (email, password, age)
POST {{api}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "bob@", "password": "123", "age": "abc" }

### 400 in Georgian: translated from code + arguments
POST {{api}}/users
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: ka

{ "email": "bob@", "password": "123", "age": "abc" }

### 409: ann@example.com is already registered
POST {{api}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ann@example.com", "password": "s3cret!pass", "age": "40" }

### 422: business rule, too young (arguments: minimumAge, age)
POST {{api}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "kid@example.com", "password": "s3cret!pass", "age": "15" }

### 200
GET {{api}}/users/ann@example.com

### 404 (arguments: email)
GET {{api}}/users/zoe@example.com

### 204, then 409 on a second call
DELETE {{api}}/users/ann@example.com

### 202 three times, then 429 with arguments.retryAfterSeconds
POST {{api}}/users/ann@example.com/password-reset

### 201 Created
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerEmail": "ann@example.com", "lines": [ { "product": "apple", "quantity": 2 }, { "product": "pear", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### 400: lines[1].product, lines[1].quantity, lines[2].quantity
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerEmail": "ann@example.com", "lines": [ { "product": "apple", "quantity": 2 }, { "product": "", "quantity": 0 }, { "product": "pear", "quantity": -1 } ] }

### 400: an order needs at least one line
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerEmail": "ann@example.com", "lines": [] }

### 404: unknown customer (field customerEmail)
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerEmail": "zoe@example.com", "lines": [ { "product": "apple", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### 403 without the admin role
GET {{api}}/admin/users

### 200 with the admin role
GET {{api}}/admin/users
X-Role: admin

### The OpenAPI document
GET {{api}}/openapi/v1.json
